Z||000000||Ralfy9862||10-31-2000||06:57 AM||||does anybody know of an after market  mufflrer for sale for the fiero preferably a glass pack design or can one be modified im just looking into the idea cause i want a louder more muscular sound. i think i seen one on a web site but i think it was for a turbo aplication. any info would help. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero56||10-31-2000||07:35 AM||||Run a search...||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||10-31-2000||08:49 AM||||Wow, that's kind of a succinct response! Really Ralfy, there are many different options for you out there, and it is a topic that has been discussed often, (and sometimes heatedly) here in this forum. If you search the archives you will find a lot of information. If you are looking for something more butch sounding, and that is your only priority, then you should be bale to get hooked up with a Thrush turbo muffler pretty cheap. If you want t really improve perfomance, you may want to upgade the exhaust system to 2.5" stainless steel.  This is where it gets expensive, but my Flowmaster does sound grrrreat! <P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||10-31-2000||08:52 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.brullenexhaust.com" TARGET=_blank>www.brullenexhaust.com</A>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  ro try to find a Powertone! they are glas packed/carbon filled muffelrs with a BEAUTIFUL sound... ||||reg||1
